    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.operator\n\n### Description\n\nIn vim-grepper, there is an gs operator for searching. for example: `gsiw`, `gsi\"`.... [ref](https://github.com/mhinz/vim-grepper/wiki/using-the-operator)\r\n\r\nI think mini.nvim can support it in minimal way:\r\nUse vim `:grep` to implement this operator, then give user an option where to put: Quickfix window or Telescope.\r\n\r\nThe advantage of implement by `:grep` is that users can use their favorite searching tools (ag, rg, ack...) by setting `grepprg`\r\n\r\n",
